/** \mainpage Four-Season Robotic Operating System - 4SROS FDE Team

@tableofcontents

@section hero Project Brief and Vision

@htmlonly
<p class="hero-lede">Our project aims to solve atmospheric ice accumulation on ski lines. This affects ski resort owners because maintaining ski lifts costs a lot of money, and delays in lift operations can affect early-bird tickets they sell for lift access; if lifts aren't ready in time, they must issue refunds. Also, under traditional protocols, mountain operations managers must call entire lift maintenance crews at 4 or 5, which costs a lot in early-morning overtime. This also affects crews, as maintenance can be dangerous and they risk slips, falls, and frostbite. Our project aims to deploy surveying robots that drastically speed up this clearance, saving ski lift resort owners money, making maintenance safer and less time-consuming, and allowing managers to make data-backed decisions about ski lift maintenance.

Success for this project looks like being able to simulate ski lift line atmospheric accumulation. A drone successfully inspects it and triggers a call to action for another robot to verify. Record and document live footage of the perception and observation of this ice accumulation in a UI so the mountain operations manager can review it and make decisions.  
..</p>
@endhtmlonly

@section  Key Outcomes and Demonstrated Results
<p class="hero-lede">The mission proceeds as follows. he Parrot drone surveys the ski-lift line using an RGB-D camera and known ski-lift geometry to identify atmospheric ice accumulation. Once it detects a potential hazard, it records its location and deploys the Husky to investigateThe Husky navigates towards reported location where along it path has various type of obstical and then using obstacle detection to identify the prioritise of that reported and/or whether the ice accumulation is hazardous...</p>

- <a href="https://youtube.com/playlist?list=PLW5p97sRPNHU&si=2CdM-c4X1aYPiS_Y">Playlist of Demonstration</a>. Live map, both cameras, and the hazard record.


@section demo_gallery Overview

@image html Environmentoverview.png "Alpine simulation: ski-lift cables, snow slope, rock gates, and the helipad"
@image html ControllerOverview.png "Operator mission interface with the live map, hazard list, and mission controls"
