---

@section results Outcomes

| Area | Result |
|---|---|
| **Perception** | Computer vision segmentation plus a 3D radial check against the cable (@f$ r_{75} \ge 0.20\,\text{m} @f$). Ground acceptance requires 4 positive frames out of 5. |
| **Planning and safety** | Lethal costmap sieve, southern corridor detours, reverse-before-turn, and bumper contact converted into a virtual laser scan. |
| **Operator** | Dual-camera view, a PyVista map of the mountain, an approve / hold / abort gate, and a SQLite record of each hazard. |
| **Verification** | Eleven pytest suites, plus `ice_evaluator.py`, which matches detections to the scenario ground truth. |

---

@section system_overview System Architecture

We split the work across three cooperating parts, all running in Ignition Gazebo Fortress.

1. **Aerial scout (Parrot UAV).** It patrols the cable spans, follows the catenary, and proposes ice candidates from a forward RGB-D camera.
2. **Ground inspector (Clearpath Husky).** It navigates the snow slope under Nav2, detours lethal rock gates, and confirms each pin with a multi-frame camera check.
3. **Operator interface.** It shows live telemetry and both cameras, holds the mission until a person approves, and writes the result to SQLite.

