@section authors Authors


Owen is a final-year student double majoring in mechanical and mechatronic engineering. His primary responsibilities were GUI development, systems integration and supporting robotic decision-making. His work focused on developing and integrating a 3D map to visualise robot and hazard locations in the GUI as well as implementing a Live operations panel displaying robotic camera feeds, perception outputs and mission activities. He also developed a Documented Hazards Panel to track detected hazards, including their locations, detection images, timestamps and intervention status.


Vu is a third-year student majoring in mechatronic and served as the team leader for this project. He primary responsibilities included project and stakeholder management, robotic perception, navigation and simulation environment development. His work focused on creating the alpine simulation environment, integrating SLAM capabilities for the Parrot drone and Husky ground robot, developing perception systems for atmospheric ice detection along ski-lift lines and implementing obstacle avoidance for the Husky.


*/
